# Parallel Sessions: Worktrees + Test Queue

Canonical workflow: `docs/workflow/parallel-sessions.md`.

## Classify the session first

At the start of a task (and when its scope turns into code changes), decide the class:

| Class | Trigger | Where |
|-------|---------|-------|
| `review` | Review a branch / PR / commit range | `..\earnie-wt\review-<slug>`, `--detach` on the reviewed ref, read-only |
| `fix` | Bugfix | `..\earnie-wt\fix-<slug>`, branch `fix/<slug>` |
| `hotfix` | Patch for a tagged build | `..\earnie-wt\hotfix-<slug>`, branch from the tag (`branching-hotfix-playbook.mdc`) |
| `feat` | Feature / refactoring with code changes | `..\earnie-wt\feat-<slug>`, branch `feat/<slug>` |
| `port` | Cherry-picks onto `release/x.y` | `..\earnie-wt\port-<slug>`, branch `port/<slug>` |
| `spike` | Throw-away experiment | `..\earnie-wt\spike-<slug>`, branch `spike/<slug>` |
| `bisect` / `compare` | Regression triage | existing worktrees of skill `regression-triage` |
| — | Docs / backlog only, Q&A without edits, release-notes drafts, session conclusion | main checkout |

- If the session already runs inside a matching worktree: just use it.
- If code changes are needed and the session is in the main checkout: create the worktree (commands in the workflow doc), tell the user the path and branch in one line, then work there. **Ask first** only if the main checkout has uncommitted changes that belong to this task (they would have to move along).
- Never `git checkout`/`switch` branches in the main checkout for these classes — other sessions and the user work there.
- Paths: next to the repo, short, never under a drive root or `.claude/worktrees/`.

## Tests

- Always via `scripts.run_pytest` / `scripts.run_regression` — they queue machine-wide (`scripts/suite_queue.py`); never plain `python -m pytest`, never `EARNIE_TEST_QUEUE=off` / `--no-queue` to jump the queue.
- In a worktree: main checkout's interpreter, started from the **worktree root**: `<earnie-root>\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m scripts.run_pytest tests -q --tb=short`.
- Full suite in Claude Code: Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` (queue wait + run can exceed the 10 min foreground limit). Targeted files/node ids (≤ 3) use the fast lane and do not queue.
- Waiting output `[test-queue] waiting …` is normal — do not kill and restart the run. `python -m scripts.suite_queue status` shows the queue.

## Finish

Commit + push the branch from the worktree; integration (PR / merge) per `branching-hotfix-playbook.mdc` and session conclusion. Remove the worktree after merge/abandon (`git worktree remove`, `git branch -d`). Shared `.venv`: dependency changes affect all sessions — coordinate with the user before installing.
